---
// Privacy Policy, aligned with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy
// Principles (APPs). It describes what this website actually does (see the notes on
// browser storage and hosting logs); keep it in step if a site adds analytics or forms.
import { features } from '../../../config/features.mjs';
import ContactBlock from './ContactBlock.astro';
import LegalPage from './LegalPage.astro';
import { info } from './legal-info';

const health = info.legal.collectsHealthInfo;
const sections = [
  { id: 'about', title: 'About this policy' },
  { id: 'collect', title: 'What we collect' },
  ...(health ? [{ id: 'health', title: 'Health information' }] : []),
  { id: 'how', title: 'How we collect it' },
  { id: 'website', title: 'This website' },
  { id: 'use', title: 'How we use it' },
  { id: 'share', title: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'ai', title: 'AI and your information' },
  { id: 'security', title: 'Storage and security' },
  { id: 'access', title: 'Access and correction' },
  { id: 'complaints', title: 'Questions and complaints' },
];
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${info.name} collects, uses and protects your personal information.`}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="about">About this policy</h2>
  <p>
    {info.legalName} ("we", "us") respects your privacy. This policy explains how we handle
    personal information under the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the Australian Privacy
    Principles. It covers our {info.services}, our communications with you and this website.
  </p>

  <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
  <p>We only collect what we need to look after you. This may include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, phone number and email address;</li>
    <li>details of your {info.services}: dates, times, preferences and payment records;</li>
    {health && <li>health information relevant to your {info.service} (see below);</li>}
    <li>anything you choose to tell us when you contact us.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You may deal with us anonymously or under a pseudonym where that's practical, for example
    when asking a general question. We'll need your name and contact details to make a booking.
  </p>

  {
    health && (
      <>
        <h2 id="health">Health information</h2>
        <p>
          Before your first {info.service}, and from time to time after, we ask about your health:
          injuries, conditions, medications, pregnancy and anything else that affects how we can
          safely care for you. Under the Privacy Act this is <strong>sensitive information</strong>,
          and we handle it with extra care:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>we only collect it with your consent, and only what is relevant to your care;</li>
          <li>
            it is seen only by the {info.practitioners} who look after you and the people who manage
            your records;
          </li>
          <li>we never use it for marketing, and never sell or trade it;</li>
          <li>
            we keep it for as long as we need it to care for you and to meet our legal obligations,
            then destroy it securely.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You don't have to share health information, but if you don't, we may not be able to
          provide a {info.service} safely.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2 id="how">How we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    Usually directly from you: in person, by phone, by email or through a booking or message. If
    someone else books for you (for example, as a gift), we'll collect your details from them and
    confirm them with you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
  <p>We keep this website private by design:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No tracking or advertising cookies</strong>, and no analytics profiling of visitors.</li>
    <li>
      If you use the music button, your choice (on or off) is saved <strong>in your own browser</strong>{' '}
      so the site remembers it. It never leaves your device, and you can clear it at any time in your
      browser settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      Our hosting provider keeps short-term technical logs (such as IP addresses and the pages
      requested) to keep the site secure and working. Where we limit repeated requests to stop abuse,
      visitor addresses are scrambled first, so the original address is not kept.
    </li>
    {
      features.turnstile && (
        <li>
          Forms on this site use Cloudflare Turnstile to block spam. It checks your browser without
          tracking you across other sites; see Cloudflare's privacy policy for details.
        </li>
      )
    }
    <li>
      Links to other services (such as maps or social media) take you to sites with their own
      privacy policies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>to book, provide and follow up your {info.services};</li>
    {health && <li>to make sure each {info.service} is safe and suitable for you;</li>}
    <li>to reply to your questions and send appointment reminders;</li>
    <li>to keep business, tax and legal records;</li>
    <li>to keep our website and systems secure.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We'll only send you news or offers if you ask for them, and every message will tell you how to
    stop.
  </p>

  <h2 id="share">Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We don't sell, rent or trade personal information. We share it only when needed with trusted
    service providers who help us run the business (such as booking, payment, email and website
    hosting services), when you ask us to, or when the law requires it (including to prevent a
    serious threat to someone's life, health or safety).
  </p>
  <p>
    Some of these providers may store or process information outside Australia, including on
    secure cloud servers overseas. When that happens we take reasonable steps to make sure they
    protect it in line with the Australian Privacy Principles.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and your information</h2>
  {
    info.legal.ai.customerDataInAI ? (
      <p>
        We use a small number of business-grade AI tools to help run our business (for example, to
        help draft replies). We only use services that keep your information confidential and do not
        use it to train their AI models, and{health && ' we never put health information into them, and'}
        a person always reviews the result.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>
        We do not put your personal{health && ' or health'} information into AI tools such as
        chatbots or AI writing assistants.
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    No decisions about you are made by automated means: your bookings and {info.services} are always
    handled by people.
    {info.legal.ai.aiChat && ' The chat assistant on this site is automated, so please don\'t share health or payment details in it.'}
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">Storage and security</h2>
  <p>
    We protect personal information from misuse, loss and unauthorised access with secure systems,
    limited access and up-to-date software. This website is served over an encrypted connection with
    strict security settings. When we no longer need information, we destroy it or remove anything
    that identifies you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="access">Access and correction</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct it, at any
    time. We'll respond within 30 days. In rare cases the law allows us to refuse; if so, we'll tell
    you why.
  </p>

  <h2 id="complaints">Questions and complaints</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a question or a concern about your privacy, please contact us first. We'll look into
    it and reply within 30 days.
  </p>
  <ContactBlock privacy />
  <p>
    If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian
    Information Commissioner at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener noreferrer">oaic.gov.au</a>{' '}
    or on 1300 363 992.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
